    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) as our premier offensive anchor. Facing McGreevy, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a prime lead-off spot and a substantial boost from the platoon advantage, making him our highest-probability source for the stolen bases we desperately need to stay competitive. Joining him at the top of the hierarchy is **Junior Caminero** (76.88), whose matchup against Quantrill is our most favorable SP_xERA environment (5.02). With an elite xwOBA of 0.371 and the protection of the three-hole, **Junior Caminero** is projected to provide the heavy lifting in HR and RBI categories. **Trea Turner** (68.96) and **Christian Yelich** (65.16) round out our strong starters, with **Trea Turner** leveraging a solid BvP history and **Christian Yelich** benefiting from favorable wind conditions at the park.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dillon Dingler** (39.01), who fell just shy of our 40.0 floor. Despite a respectable 0.381 xwOBA, the negative impact of facing Kremer in a platoon-disadvantaged spot dragged his efficiency score down, forcing us to favor the versatility of **Caleb Durbin** (56.66) in the UTIL slot. We are also closely monitoring the high-leverage risk surrounding **Yordan Alvarez** (56.32); while his raw power is undeniable, he faces a difficult matchup against the lefty Detmers, which significantly dampens his projection compared to his usual ceiling. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** remains sidelined, and we continue to track the development of **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors, hoping for a call-up that would bolster our middle infield depth. With **Colt Keith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Josh Smith** providing necessary coverage, our focus remains on maximizing plate appearances against sub-4.50 xERA arms to maintain our Roto standing.",
